"""Session 11. The business case. A worked example: the NVF Monday sales email costed in the Business Case Workbook, the Session 8 message workflow with invented volumes,
and the F6 invoice check as a second example (two real AI runs against invoice_errors_key.csv and a recomputation from supplier_invoices.csv).

Rebuilt 4 November 2026 (author e). Where the numbers come from:
 - Baseline: the Session 1 task card (slide 'A finished task card from Nile Valley Foods' in s01.py): 90 minutes, 4 a month, errors in 4 runs out of 10, UGX 150,000 an error, draft ready in 10 minutes and checked in 20, E or M marks.
 - ONE set of numbers, aligned on the task card: minutes with the tool 10 (the card's 'draft in 10 minutes'), review 20. The workbook default Inputs!B12 is now 10 (changed 4 Nov 2026), so the template reproduces these figures.
 - Costs and results: the grey NVF values of Templates/Business Case Workbook.xlsx (licence UGX 60,000 a month and UGX 30,000 an hour are INVENTED, as the workbook says). Recomputed by script from the workbook formulas with B12 = 10:
   time saved 4 x 80 min x 30,000 = 160,000; errors avoided 144,000; monthly benefit 304,000; monthly cost 145,000 (licence 60,000 + review 40,000 + upkeep 45,000); monthly net 159,000; one-off 480,000; payback 3.0 months; 12-month net 1,428,000;
   at a 30% haircut 333,600; break-even haircut about 39%; low -80,980 (12-month -1,595,760); high 270,780 (1.6 months, 12-month 2,817,360).
 - Message workflow: ALL figures INVENTED for the arithmetic, including the baseline of 45 minutes a day (an example row on the Session 1 practice slide, never measured; the Session 8 deck calls it an invented example): 20 days a month, UGX 30,000 an hour,
   running costs 105,000 a month (licence 60,000 + upkeep 45,000; the person’s minutes are the varied column), UGX 480,000 once, person minutes with the workflow 15, 25 and 35 a day (Session 8 did not measure them). Labelled on the slide.
 - Invoice check: Case Runs/runs/F6_invoice_check_run1.md and _run2.md, Claude, a fresh session given only the prompt, 4 November 2026, answer key hidden. Amounts recomputed from supplier_invoices.csv (60 rows, 59 distinct invoices, so 51 are not flagged).
No vendor prices are used.
"""

