              'Invoice check results. What is recorded: two Claude sessions, each a fresh session given only the prompt, 4 November 2026, answer key hidden; the runs were agent sessions that read one prompt file and wrote an answer file. Files: 05 Course Maintenance/Case Runs/runs/F6_invoice_check_run1.md and F6_invoice_check_run2.md, prompt in Case Runs/prompts/F6_invoice_check.md, key in 04 Facilitator Materials/Answer Keys/invoice_errors_key.csv. Say whose result it is: Claude, not ChatGPT or Gemini, two runs, another day or product may differ. The prompt did not call the invoices fictional, but the file is a teaching file.',
              'What the runs did (both read in full and compared with the key and with a recomputation of supplier_invoices.csv, 60 rows): both found all 8 problems (4 wrong totals, 2 missing purchase order numbers, 1 duplicate TR-2026-0093, and the 0% VAT invoice LL-2026-0464 as unsure). No false alarms in either run: the look-alike repeat trips (LL-2026-0446 and 0458, LL-2026-0455 and 0476) and the correct repeat PP-2026-0165 were rightly not flagged as errors. Neither run explained PP-2026-0174 as an older, lower unit price; run 2 pointed out that the same item on PP-2026-0156 was priced right. Both said they did the sums by hand without a calculator or code (their own statement, which cannot be checked). Run 2 said dates and PO numbers were in sequence, which is not quite true (the duplicate row repeats PO-2026-1310 out of order), a small overclaim.',
